; Local config for DK_Sync.ahk. Copy to C:\FSBHOA\dk_sync.ini on the RAM PC.
; Keep this file on the PC's LOCAL disk, never on the NAS.
; Values must be bare (IniRead does not strip inline comments).
;
; Environment  : testbed | production. Selects the watch folder To_RAM_Testbed / To_RAM_Production
;                and must match env= in the trigger file.
; ExpectedHost : host name of the Access Control server allowed to trigger this PC
;                (testbed.fsbhoa.com or the production host). Must match host= in the trigger file.
; BaseDir      : NAS folder as mapped on this PC.
; GateAccounts : optional. The script sends to every account in RAM's Send Data Now list and,
;                by default, waits for each to report success. If RAM also lists an account
;                whose panel can't be reached (a test account), name the accounts that must
;                report here, comma-separated, as RAM names them; the others' results are
;                then only logged. Not needed in production, where RAM lists only North Gates
;                and South Gates. (GateRowsY, the rows' screen positions, is no longer used.)
;
; Optional, for the vehicle plugin, which reads RAM's Live Streaming Disk File
; (BaseDir\Live_<Environment>\stream.txt):
; RamWatch        : 1 to check every 60 seconds that RAM is running, start it if not, and write
;                   the heartbeat ram_pc_status.txt in that folder for the vehicle settings
;                   page. Default 0 (off).
; RamPath         : full path of DoorKing32.exe. Optional: the script notes it while RAM runs.
; SendTimeoutSeconds : optional. How long an import waits for RAM's record that the send to
;                   the panels finished (in Live_<Environment>\stream.txt). Default 300; raise
;                   it if the panels' link is slow (production's is cellular).

[DK_Sync]
Environment=testbed
ExpectedHost=testbed.fsbhoa.com
BaseDir=Y:\Automation\DoorKing
RamWatch=1
